# A contact manifold describing the contact points between colliding
# shapes, ported from upstream b2Manifold in collision.h. Box2D uses
# speculative collision so some contact points may be separated.
#
# Collision functions write into existing manifolds (the To-forms), so a
# warm loop reuses one Manifold and allocates nothing. Every geometry field
# is overwritten on each call.
Class Manifold
## The unit normal vector in world space, pointing from shape A to shape B.
## Zero when the manifold is empty.
Property Normal As Vector2

## Angular impulse applied for rolling resistance. N * m * s.
Property RollingImpulse As Double

## First manifold point. Only meaningful when PointCount is at least one.
Property Point1 As ManifoldPoint

## Second manifold point. Only meaningful when PointCount is two.
Property Point2 As ManifoldPoint

## The number of contact points: 0, 1, or 2.
Property PointCount As Integer

## Lazily created reusable workspace for collision functions.
Property mScratch As CollideScratch

## Creates an empty manifold.
Constructor()
Me.Normal = New Vector2(0.0, 0.0)
Me.RollingImpulse = 0.0
Me.Point1 = New ManifoldPoint
Me.Point2 = New ManifoldPoint
Me.PointCount = 0
# The collision scratch is created eagerly so a pooled manifold never
# allocates on its first narrow-phase use: pool objects are recycled into
# rows that may collide in the same step they are adopted, and a lazy
# scratch would push the allocation into a measured zero-allocation step
# window.
Me.mScratch = New CollideScratch
End Constructor

## Resets the manifold to the empty state in place and returns it.
Function Reset() As Manifold
Me.Normal.Set(0.0, 0.0)
Me.RollingImpulse = 0.0
Me.Point1.Reset()
Me.Point2.Reset()
Me.PointCount = 0
Return Me
End Function

## Copies every field from another manifold into this one, including the
## full contact points. Used to snapshot manifolds for events.
Sub AssignFrom(other As Manifold)
Me.Normal.Set(other.Normal.X, other.Normal.Y)
Me.RollingImpulse = other.RollingImpulse
Me.Point1.AssignFrom(other.Point1)
Me.Point2.AssignFrom(other.Point2)
Me.PointCount = other.PointCount
End Sub

## Returns the lazily created reusable workspace. Engine code only.
Function Scratch() As CollideScratch
If Me.mScratch = Nothing Then
Me.mScratch = New CollideScratch
End If
Return Me.mScratch
End Function
End Class
